map_choice_ignored.description:
Battman now uses these entities by name, so what you picked for them on its Configure screen no longer applies:

{choices}

If the entity Battman now uses is right, clear your choice: open Battman → Configure and set it back to that entity (if it's no longer listed there, just save). If your entity has a different name, rename it to the one Battman uses (Settings → Entities). This notice goes once nothing is left to clear.

integration_too_old.description:
Battman uses entity names that only exist from these versions on:

{old}

Update it in HACS, then restart Home Assistant. (If its entities were created by an older version, they may still have older names: Battman's missing-entities Repair names any it can't find.)

missing_entities.description:
Battman uses these entities by name, and they aren't available:

{missing}

Install or enable the integration named, or enable the entity under Settings → Entities. If it exists under a different name, rename it to the name above. Until then, what uses it shows a note or a blank (never a made-up value).

missing_dependencies.description:
Battman's dashboard uses things that aren't installed. Install them with HACS (cards under Frontend; browser_mod as an integration, then add it under Settings → Devices & services), then restart Home Assistant and refresh your browser:

{missing}

The full list is in DEPENDENCIES.md in the Battman repository.
